# Saving a binary response body to a file instead of rendering it -- the
# "# @download" annotation below saves the body byte-for-byte under
# .httpfly/downloads/ (bare "# @download" names the file after the URL's
# last path segment; "# @download name.ext" sets it explicitly). The result
# pane shows the saved path in place of the body. See 7_save_response.http
# for saving a response body yourself from a post-request script instead.
#
# Run `make httpbin-up` first.

###
# @name GetPNG
# @download photo.png
GET http://localhost:8080/image/png HTTP/1.1
Accept: image/png
